<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Interesting post, thank you! I tested it and except that I had to strip non-word characters out of the values, it mostly works - it doesn't pick up the &lt;c&gt;id&lt;/c&gt; of the &lt;strike&gt;&lt;c&gt;Sunday&lt;/c&gt;&lt;/strike&gt; &lt;c&gt;Saturday&lt;/c&gt; entry, and it also picks up the values "&lt;c&gt;bbbdddeeeggg&lt;/c&gt;", but overall it's a very interesting start. Regexes are a fine tool for lexing, and by adding some logic around them keeping track of the nested tags etc., it's basically like building a simple parser.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
